    "note": "Empty-arena variant of generic-goal-navigation for the real-OriginBot canary: the imu-gravity-v1 42D observation carries no obstacle signal and the board runtime supplies none either, so obstacle avoidance is structurally out of contract. The deployed scenario is an operator-cleared floor, which this task models exactly; actuator lag/slip/bias domain randomization is unchanged and is what sim2real robustness is actually judged on. Trained in simulation only; real-board acceptance is the low-speed canary itself."
